column41:
1.Login 2,3 client and admin on same server.
[2.Do|http://2.Do] trades with all dealers.
3.Take online and Generic backup.
4.You will see that,while taking backup on any one dealer-> in backup file all trades of all dealer's get print.

*Observation:Issue is from Arjun's patch date:22/12/2025 11:22pm*



{color:#403294}+*Developer comment*+{color}

{color:#403294}Please check backup path for all clients…{color}

{color:#403294}It will never happen that one dealer will get trades of another dealers,{color}

{color:#403294}+*This will happen incase of Admin user only…*+{color}

{color:#403294}So please verify your backup path if you are running multiple clients on same machine{color}

{color:#403294}Regards,{color}

{color:#403294}Bhushan R Chaudhari{color}

h2. 

h2. {color:#bf2600}*As per our analysis, it is issue related to downloading,*{color}

h2. {color:#bf2600}*User is getting downloading for data of user id: HANU123 even if user is login with user id: SAYALI,*{color}

h2. {color:#bf2600}*In case of online trade user is not getting online trades for HANU123 where as can get online trades for user id: SAYALI which is correct in flow*{color}

h2. Regards,

Bhushan

!image-20260106-064853.png|width=1131,alt="image-20260106-064853.png"!

When the _Get Market Status_ API is called in the UAT environment, the response returns market status information twice for NSE EQ and twice for NSE FO. This results in duplicate or multiple status entries for the same exchange segments within a single API response. 

Also note, MemberId and UserId for both NSE-EQ and NSE-FO is Same for the UAT Environment

