Purpose of POC is to try and verify following: 

# To verify and check that two producers from different GETS manager servers can write on same Subject of NATS+Jetstream, this data to be consumed by stateless Service on GNexLayer and identify packets broker and insert/update in correct partition/index of Redis assigned to that Broker during onboarding.
# Any change in Users data in GNexLayer to be written to correct subject of NATS as identified by new field added in users data. This new field is identifier for the GETS Manger server. The consumer on respective GETS Manager reads from that Subject/Topic and updates in GETS Manager.

Use following structure and Mock programs to implement additional components, Also since this is POC just print output on screen after executing necessary logic in code. It may not be required to do actual updates in DB or Redis just to save upon time.

Sample structures:

{noformat}// GNLDataSyncMsgHeader represents the header structure for syncup messages between GETS Manager and GNexLayer
struct GNLDataSyncMsgHeader {
    int16_t MessageCode;     // Equivalent to Go's int16
    int32_t MessageLength;   // Equivalent to Go's int32
    char strBrokerTag[size]    // We will introduce Broker tag here to identify to which Broker this clients data belongs.
    int32_t TimeStamp;       // Equivalent to Go's int32
    int32_t Reserved;        // Equivalent to Go's int32
};{noformat}

{noformat}struct UserData {
    GNLDataSyncMsgHeader  ObjGNLDataSyncMsgHeader;
    long lMobileNo = 0;
    char chGscId[CorePacketFieldSize::GscId] = {0};

    char chGETSServerIdentifier[10] = { 0 }; //New add for GETS server identifier, this will help it in routing orders to correct backend GETS server.
                                            //Sample values: "1A" or "1B"
};{noformat}



