column41:
If the external orders/trade identifier is specified in CTCLManager.ini, the same will be sent by the client communicator to the client when downloading is complete.

The client will then update its records for the same and treat every greek message which has the identifier present in ‘Strategy name’ field as an ‘external order / trade’

External orders are dormant cannot be modified or cancelled, even though product conversion is allowed.



+*CTCLManager.ini Feature Flag Details:*+

StrategyName = ‘MOSL’



Example: Orders coming in from Motilal Oswal other trading terminal are flagged as ‘MOSL’ in the ‘Strategy Name’ field.





In response, will send data in following structure,

struct STRATEGY_DETAILS
{
    GREEK_HEADER    objGreek_Header;
    char cStrategyName[26] = {0};
};

Transcodes for request/response,

h1. define GC_STRATEGY_INFO_REQ                       16953

h1. define GC_STRATEGY_INFO_RES                       16954

h1. 📘 *Console_rhl8 – Offline Order Setting Guide*

This document outlines how to configure offline order settings in {{CTCLManager.ini}} using the {{OfflineOrderCodeTune}} flag.

----

h2. 🔹 *1. Send Offline by Market Status (*{{OfflineOrderCodeTune = 0}}*)*

{quote}*Purpose:* Send offline orders to the exchange based on market status.{quote}

* The market status is receiving from the *Broadcast Application* or *CTCL Manager*.

h3. ✅ Important Notes:

# *Dependency on TBT contracts & security files*:
#* {{m_contract_stream_info.csv}}
#* {{fo_contract_stream_info.csv}}
#* {{cd_contract_stream_info.csv}}

----

h2. 🔹 *2. Send Offline Order Before Market (*{{OfflineOrderCodeTune = 1}}*)*

{quote}*Purpose:* Send orders _before_ market opening time.{quote}

h3. 🛠 Configuration in {{CTCLManager.ini}}:

{noformat}OfflineOrderCodeTune = 1
AllowOfflineOrderRecurrence = true
IsOfflineOrderByPass = false
RecurrenceOrderCount = 1000
{noformat}

h3. 🕒 NSE EQ Settings:

# {{NSEEQ_PREOPEN_OFFLINE=090000}}
# {{NSEEQ_PREOPEN_OFFLINE_ADV=380}}
# {{NSEEQ_OFFLINE=091500}}
# {{NSEEQ_OFFLINE_ADV=380}}
# {{NSEEQ_POSTCLOSE_OFFLINE=154000}}
# {{NSEEQ_PREOPEN_OFFLINE_ADV=380}}

h3. 🕒 NSE FO Settings:

# {{NSEFO_OFFLINE=091500}}
# {{NSEFO_OFFLINE_ADV=380}}

h3. 🕒 NSE CD Settings:

# {{NSECD_OFFLINE=090000}}
# {{NSECD_OFFLINE_ADV=380}}

h3. ✅ Important Notes:

# Server time must be synchronized with the Exchange.
# Dependency on TBT contracts & security files:
#* {{m_contract_stream_info.csv}}
#* {{fo_contract_stream_info.csv}}
#* {{cd_contract_stream_info.csv}}

----

h2. 🔹 *3. Send Offline Order After Time Match (*{{OfflineOrderCodeTune = 2}}*)*

{quote}*Purpose:* Orders sent after specific set times match (supports microsecond precision).{quote}

h3. 🛠 Configuration in {{CTCLManager.ini}}:

{noformat}OfflineOrderCodeTune = 2
AllowOfflineOrderRecurrence = true
IsOfflineOrderByPass = false
RecurrenceOrderCount = 1000
{noformat}

h3. 🕒 NSE EQ Settings:

# {{NSEEQ_PREOPEN_OFFLINE=085959}}
# {{NSEEQ_OFFLINE_FIRST_ORDER=085958}}
# {{NSEEQ_PREOPEN_MICRO_SEC=999500}}
# {{NSEEQ_OFFLINE=091459}}
# {{NSEEQ_OPEN_MICRO_SEC=999500}}
# {{NSEEQ_OPEN_OFFLINE_FIRST_ORDER=091458}}
# {{NSEEQ_POSTCLOSE_OFFLINE=153959}}
# {{NSEEQ_POST_CLOSE_OFFLINE_FIRST_ORDER=153958}}
# {{NSEEQ_POST_CLOSE_OPEN_MICRO_SEC=999500}}

h3. 🕒 NSE FO Settings:

# {{NSEFO_OFFLINE=091500}}
# {{NSEFO_OFFLINE_FIRST_ORDER=091458}}
# {{NSEFO_OFFLINE_MICRO_SEC=999500}}

h3. 🕒 NSE CD Settings:

# {{NSECD_OFFLINE=090000}}
# {{NSECD_OFFLINE_FIRST_ORDER=085958}}
# {{NSECD_OFFLINE_MICRO_SEC=999500}}

h3. ✅ Important Notes:

# Message rate must be more than *8 messages per second*.
# Server time must be synchronized with the Exchange.

----

h2. 🔹 *4. Send Offline Order Stream-Wise (*{{OfflineOrderCodeTune = 3}}*)*

{quote}*Purpose:* Orders are sent *per stream* after time match, synchronized by NSE Interactive.{quote}

h3. 🛠 Configuration in {{CTCLManager.ini}}:

{noformat}OfflineOrderCodeTune = 3
AllowOfflineOrderRecurrence = true
IsOfflineOrderByPass = false
RecurrenceOrderCount = 1000
{noformat}

h3. 🕒 NSE EQ Settings:

# {{NSEEQ_PREOPEN_OFFLINE=085959}}
# {{NSEEQ_OFFLINE_FIRST_ORDER=085958}}
# {{NSEEQ_PREOPEN_MICRO_SEC=999500}}
# {{NSEEQ_OFFLINE=091459}}
# {{NSEEQ_OPEN_MICRO_SEC=999500}}
# {{NSEEQ_OPEN_OFFLINE_FIRST_ORDER=091458}}
# {{NSEEQ_POSTCLOSE_OFFLINE=153959}}
# {{NSEEQ_POST_CLOSE_OFFLINE_FIRST_ORDER=153958}}
# {{NSEEQ_POST_CLOSE_OPEN_MICRO_SEC=999500}}

h3. 🕒 NSE FO Settings:

# {{NSEFO_OFFLINE=091500}}
# {{NSEFO_OFFLINE_FIRST_ORDER=091458}}
# {{NSEFO_OFFLINE_MICRO_SEC=999500}}

h3. 🕒 NSE CD Settings:

# {{NSECD_OFFLINE=090000}}
# {{NSECD_OFFLINE_FIRST_ORDER=085958}}
# {{NSECD_OFFLINE_MICRO_SEC=999500}}

h3. ✅ Important Notes:

# Message rate must be more than:
#* *Number of Streams × 5 messages/sec*
_Example: If 9 streams in NSE EQ → 9 × 5 = 45 messages per second_
# Server time must be synchronized with the Exchange.

----

h2. 📎 Summary Table

||Mode||Flag Value||Trigger Mechanism||Notes|| ||
|0|{{0}}|Based on Market Status|Requires TBT contracts and files| |
|1|{{1}}|Fixed pre-market time|Time sync required| |
|2|{{2}}|Matched timestamp (microsecond)|all stream offline order submit by single event.| |
|3|{{3}}|Per-stream timestamp|Message rate = stream × 5| |

----

